WEBVTT

1
00:00:26.166 --> 00:00:30.333


2
00:00:30.333 --> 00:00:31.208
<b>Here,</b>

3
00:00:31.208 --> 00:00:32.291
<b>Lord Krishna,</b>

4
00:00:32.291 --> 00:00:36.250
<b>while talking about human experiences, says,</b>

5
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:38.375
<b>"O son of Kunti, Arjuna,</b>

6
00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:40.458
<b>it is our senses</b>

7
00:00:40.458 --> 00:00:46.375
<b>that generate the experiences of cold and heat,</b>
<b>pleasure and pain within us.</b>

8
00:00:46.375 --> 00:00:51.916
<b>In this transient, impermanent world,</b>
<b>such experiences never remain constant;</b>

9
00:00:51.916 --> 00:00:54.625
<b>they change with time.</b>

10
00:00:54.625 --> 00:00:55.791
<b>O Bharat,</b>

11
00:00:55.791 --> 00:00:58.375
<b>learn to endure them."</b>

12
00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:03.166


13
00:01:03.166 --> 00:01:06.666
<b>Lord Krishna is highlighting here that</b>

14
00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:15.000
<b>it is wise to learn to endure those events and</b>
<b>experiences over which we have no control.</b>

15
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.041
<b>Arjuna might be thinking,</b>

16
00:01:17.041 --> 00:01:17.916
<b>"Yes,</b>

17
00:01:17.916 --> 00:01:19.000
<b>I agree</b>

18
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.291
<b>that our existence is the soul, </b>

19
00:01:21.291 --> 00:01:22.250
<b>but</b>

20
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:27.125
<b>when I or any loved one leaves this body,</b>

21
00:01:27.125 --> 00:01:32.416
<b>it is natural to feel immense pain</b>
<b>and sorrow, isn't it?"</b>

22
00:01:32.416 --> 00:01:37.083
<b>This is the very concern that</b>
<b>Krishna is trying to address.</b>

23
00:01:37.083 --> 00:01:38.958
<b>His implication is that</b>

24
00:01:38.958 --> 00:01:39.791
<b>yes,</b>

25
00:01:39.791 --> 00:01:41.250
<b>pain is natural,</b>

26
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.000
<b>but</b>

27
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.625
<b>if we completely lose control</b>
<b>over our experiences,</b>

28
00:01:46.625 --> 00:01:49.291
<b>we will be utterly entangled.</b>

29
00:01:49.291 --> 00:01:51.291
<b>For this control, it is necessary</b>

30
00:01:51.291 --> 00:01:55.416
<b>to first understand that such sorrow is futile,</b>

31
00:01:55.416 --> 00:02:00.708
<b>and when we know this truth,</b>
<b>perhaps the pain will not vanish instantly,</b>

32
00:02:00.708 --> 00:02:03.333
<b>the sorrow will not dissolve immediately,</b>

33
00:02:03.333 --> 00:02:03.958
<b>but</b>

34
00:02:03.958 --> 00:02:09.541
<b>this very awareness will certainly help</b>
<b>in reducing this pain and sorrow.</b>

35
00:02:09.541 --> 00:02:12.333
<b>And then, after continuous effort, </b>

36
00:02:12.333 --> 00:02:13.958
<b>a time will also come</b>

37
00:02:13.958 --> 00:02:18.916
<b>when we will have so much control</b>
<b>over these experiences, these senses,</b>

38
00:02:18.916 --> 00:02:23.250
<b>that we will be able to rise above such misery.</b>

39
00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:27.625
<b>Just as the first step is essential</b>
<b>to reach somewhere,</b>

40
00:02:27.625 --> 00:02:31.291
<b>this is a first step of awareness,</b>

41
00:02:31.291 --> 00:02:35.875
<b>for complete control over</b>
<b>experiences in this transient world.</b>

42
00:02:35.875 --> 00:02:37.916
<b>Lord Krishna wants to convey</b>

43
00:02:37.916 --> 00:02:40.041
<b>that when an eternal soul</b>

44
00:02:40.041 --> 00:02:43.958
<b>begins to attach itself to this ephemeral world,</b>

45
00:02:43.958 --> 00:02:45.916
<b>that's where the</b>

46
00:02:45.916 --> 00:02:47.083
<b>delusion,</b>

47
00:02:47.083 --> 00:02:48.333
<b>sadness,</b>

48
00:02:48.333 --> 00:02:49.416
<b>and</b>

49
00:02:49.416 --> 00:02:50.750
<b>sorrow are born.</b>

50
00:02:51.458 --> 00:02:55.708


51
00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:59.500
<b>It must have happened many times</b>

52
00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:04.791
<b>when something bad</b>
<b>occurred that you didn't expect,</b>

53
00:03:04.791 --> 00:03:05.666
<b>or</b>

54
00:03:05.666 --> 00:03:10.750
<b>someone whom you considered</b>
<b>your relative, your well-wisher,</b>

55
00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:16.208
<b>suddenly displayed a</b>
<b>completely opposite nature.</b>

56
00:03:16.208 --> 00:03:20.541
<b>It must have been painful in such situations;</b>

57
00:03:20.541 --> 00:03:23.166
<b>it happens with everyone.</b>

58
00:03:23.166 --> 00:03:26.791
<b>So, what should be done in such cases?</b>

59
00:03:26.791 --> 00:03:31.000
<b>The magnitude of this pain is directly connected</b>

60
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.833
<b>to your hopes</b>

61
00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:35.666
<b>and expectations.</b>

62
00:03:35.666 --> 00:03:41.416
<b>It's not that wrong situations or</b>
<b>wrong people won't come into life.</b>

63
00:03:41.416 --> 00:03:44.833
<b>We know this well.</b>

64
00:03:44.833 --> 00:03:47.208
<b>The real problem arises</b>

65
00:03:47.208 --> 00:03:52.458
<b>when we ignore this truth</b>
<b>of the world and expect</b>

66
00:03:52.458 --> 00:03:58.416
<b>only happiness, only good situations.</b>

67
00:03:58.416 --> 00:04:04.750
<b>If this expectation reduces,</b>
<b>the pain will also reduce.</b>

68
00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:10.500
<b>By doing so, we will never drown</b>
<b>in the depths of sorrow,</b>

69
00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:15.208
<b>nor will we be deluded by</b>
<b>the heights of happiness.</b>

70
00:04:15.208 --> 00:04:22.500
<b>For a balanced life, to increase</b>
<b>our tolerance in adverse circumstances,</b>

71
00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:25.916
<b>this thinking is necessary.</b>

72
00:04:25.916 --> 00:04:28.375
<b>We must understand</b>

73
00:04:28.375 --> 00:04:31.083
<b>that life's external circumstances,</b>

74
00:04:31.083 --> 00:04:32.583
<b>other people,</b>

75
00:04:32.583 --> 00:04:36.583
<b>were never and will never be in our control.</b>

76
00:04:36.583 --> 00:04:38.291
<b>Our control</b>

77
00:04:38.291 --> 00:04:41.125
<b>is only over our thinking.</b>

78
00:04:41.125 --> 00:04:49.458
<b>In the face of any situation or any person,</b>
<b>our control is only over our given reaction.</b>

79
00:04:49.458 --> 00:04:51.666
<b>My existence is infinite,</b>

80
00:04:51.666 --> 00:04:52.500
<b>but</b>

81
00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.500
<b>my troubles are momentary;</b>

82
00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:59.875
<b>this thought will be helpful</b>
<b>in increasing resilience.</b>

83
00:04:59.875 --> 00:05:01.291
<b>However,</b>

84
00:05:01.291 --> 00:05:10.125
<b>here, tolerance does not mean enduring</b>
<b>someone's cruelty or injustice.</b>

85
00:05:10.125 --> 00:05:11.875
<b>Dharma is supreme,</b>

86
00:05:11.875 --> 00:05:16.375
<b>and tolerance towards adharma is never right.</b>

87
00:05:16.375 --> 00:05:17.375
<b>In such cases,</b>

88
00:05:17.375 --> 00:05:19.791
<b>self-defense is necessary;</b>

89
00:05:19.791 --> 00:05:23.041
<b>struggle is necessary.</b>

90
00:05:23.041 --> 00:05:24.208
<b>But</b>

91
00:05:24.208 --> 00:05:26.500
<b>how to determine this?</b>

92
00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:28.791
<b>When to be tolerant,</b>

93
00:05:28.791 --> 00:05:31.625
<b>when to struggle?</b>

94
00:05:31.625 --> 00:05:36.250
<b>Is this question arising in your mind?</b>

95
00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:38.458
<b>Don't worry,</b>

96
00:05:38.458 --> 00:05:42.000
<b>as you adopt this Gita,</b>

97
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.083
<b>the answer to every question</b>

98
00:05:44.083 --> 00:05:46.041
<b>will be found.</b>

99
00:05:46.625 --> 00:05:50.750


100
00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:53.666
<b>Sometimes in a family,</b>

101
00:05:53.666 --> 00:05:58.541
<b>it becomes extremely difficult to handle</b>
<b>a person's behavior.</b>

102
00:05:58.541 --> 00:06:01.791
<b>No matter how much affection you show,</b>

103
00:06:01.791 --> 00:06:06.750
<b>how much you try to explain</b>
<b>or understand them,</b>

104
00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:10.750
<b>there is no change.</b>

105
00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:15.958
<b>It's hard to understand what to do</b>
<b>in such situations.</b>

106
00:06:15.958 --> 00:06:18.333
<b>You should know</b>

107
00:06:18.333 --> 00:06:22.875
<b>that not all problems in life can be solved,</b>

108
00:06:22.875 --> 00:06:24.916
<b>and the truth is,</b>

109
00:06:24.916 --> 00:06:29.958
<b>not all problems in life need to be solved either.</b>

110
00:06:29.958 --> 00:06:35.083
<b>If that person is not changing</b>
<b>even after all attempts,</b>

111
00:06:35.083 --> 00:06:39.791
<b>then only one solution remains: </b>

112
00:06:39.791 --> 00:06:44.375
<b>how do we increase our tolerance</b>

113
00:06:44.375 --> 00:06:45.125
<b>and</b>

114
00:06:45.125 --> 00:06:51.000
<b>how do we protect ourselves</b>
<b>from their negative influence?</b>

115
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.833
<b>This is the only thing in your control now.</b>

116
00:06:54.833 --> 00:06:55.916
<b>Their thoughts,</b>

117
00:06:55.916 --> 00:06:57.708
<b>their destiny,</b>

118
00:06:57.708 --> 00:07:02.208
<b>you can now only strengthen yourself.</b>

119
00:07:02.208 --> 00:07:07.000
<b>If you look at it, this situation</b>
<b>also gives you something;</b>

120
00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.416
<b>it increases your tolerance,</b>

121
00:07:09.416 --> 00:07:12.833
<b>it teaches you this big lesson</b>

122
00:07:12.833 --> 00:07:17.708
<b>that you have to stay miles away from</b>
<b>such negative behavior yourself.</b>

123
00:07:17.708 --> 00:07:22.250
<b>Even a negative person teaches you</b>
<b>something before leaving.</b>

124
00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:25.250
<b>So why the sorrow?</b>

125
00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:30.375
<b>If you adopt such thinking,</b>
<b>it will make you mature.</b>

126
00:07:30.375 --> 00:07:34.208
<b>It will move you towards spirituality.</b>

127
00:07:34.208 --> 00:07:35.291
<b>Gradually,</b>

128
00:07:35.291 --> 00:07:41.791
<b>you will start to know that although many things</b>
<b>in life are not in your control,</b>

129
00:07:41.791 --> 00:07:44.791
<b>everything is still in your control.</b>

130
00:07:44.791 --> 00:07:45.541
<b>Because</b>

131
00:07:45.541 --> 00:07:49.208
<b>your reaction is in your control.</b>

132
00:07:49.208 --> 00:07:53.416
<b>Taking a positive lesson from</b>
<b>a negative situation,</b>

133
00:07:53.416 --> 00:07:56.041
<b>this is in your control.</b>

134
00:07:56.041 --> 00:07:59.041
<b>And this tolerance, this gentleness,</b>

135
00:07:59.041 --> 00:08:05.250
<b>is further strengthened by this fundamental</b>
<b>thought that all problems are temporary,</b>

136
00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:08.208
<b>but you, in the form of the soul,are constant,</b>

137
00:08:08.208 --> 00:08:09.166
<b>infinite,</b>

138
00:08:09.166 --> 00:08:11.583
<b>above all these.</b>

139
00:08:12.166 --> 00:08:16.083


140
00:08:16.083 --> 00:08:20.625
<b>Ups and downs are certain in professional life.</b>

141
00:08:20.625 --> 00:08:25.500
<b>Many times, these fluctuations</b>
<b>are not in our control;</b>

142
00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:31.208
<b>it's not in our control how others behave, </b>

143
00:08:31.208 --> 00:08:36.291
<b>whether you will receive praise or reward,</b>
<b>that's also not certain,</b>

144
00:08:36.291 --> 00:08:38.416
<b>not in control.</b>

145
00:08:38.416 --> 00:08:39.375
<b>But</b>

146
00:08:39.375 --> 00:08:41.541
<b>if nothing is certain,</b>

147
00:08:41.541 --> 00:08:43.208
<b>not in control?</b>

148
00:08:43.208 --> 00:08:46.666
<b>Should everything be abandoned?</b>

149
00:08:46.666 --> 00:08:47.791
<b>No,</b>

150
00:08:47.791 --> 00:08:52.916
<b> you may not have direct control over</b>
<b>any professional situation or person,</b>

151
00:08:52.916 --> 00:08:53.708
<b>but</b>

152
00:08:53.708 --> 00:08:56.958
<b>showing tolerance in that situation,</b>

153
00:08:56.958 --> 00:08:58.500
<b>not getting disturbed,</b>

154
00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:03.000
<b>trying to have a good influence on a person,</b>

155
00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:06.375
<b>that is certainly in your control.</b>

156
00:09:06.375 --> 00:09:08.041
<b>So, just</b>

157
00:09:08.041 --> 00:09:11.166
<b>keep doing what is in your control,</b>

158
00:09:11.166 --> 00:09:14.083
<b>and what is not in your control,</b>

159
00:09:14.083 --> 00:09:20.625
<b>just walk through the midst of</b>
<b>any such adverse situation with a smile.</b>

160
00:09:20.625 --> 00:09:23.416
<b>No matter how bad the situation is,</b>

161
00:09:23.416 --> 00:09:25.875
<b>it will certainly change.</b>

162
00:09:25.875 --> 00:09:27.625
<b>Be assured,</b>

163
00:09:27.625 --> 00:09:31.041
<b>don't consider your problems permanent.</b>

164
00:09:31.041 --> 00:09:36.291
<b>Maintain your spirituality in life and remember,</b>

165
00:09:36.291 --> 00:09:38.916
<b>no matter what the time is like,</b>

166
00:09:38.916 --> 00:09:40.708
<b>it passes.</b>

